    <div class="bio-with-sidebar">
      <div class="bio-main">
        <p>Dr. Tal Lavian, Ph.D. (UC Berkeley, Computer Science), is a telecommunications consultant and inventor of 120+ patents, specializing in <a href="/communications-expert-witness/data-communications-expert-witness/">data communications</a>, <a href="/communications-expert-witness/computer-networking-expert-witness/">computer networks</a>, and <a href="/communications-expert-witness/internet-expert-witness/">internet protocols (TCP/IP)</a>. He has been retained in 90+ cases, with 60+ depositions, and has filed declarations in more than 90 PTAB proceedings (IPR and CBM).</p>

        <p>He spent nearly 20 years researching, studying, and lecturing at UC Berkeley, including as Industry Fellow and Lecturer in the IEOR Department and SCET. He was Principal Scientist and Principal Architect at Nortel Networks (1996&ndash;2007), and Principal Investigator for three DARPA projects, including one for the U.S. Air Force Research Lab.</p>

        <p>He has co-authored over 25 <a href="/scientific-publications/">scientific publications and peer-reviewed papers</a> (<a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=DDVtnHEAAAAJ" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Scholar</a>) and is the <a href="https://patents.justia.com/inventor/tal-lavian" target="_blank" rel="noopener">inventor</a> of over 120 <a href="/patents/">issued and filed patents</a>, more than 60 of them prosecuted pro se before the USPTO. He is an IEEE Senior Member.</p>
      </div>
